{"name":"The Rainbow Fish","hex":"#4466ee","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rainbow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A multicoloured arch in the sky, produced by prismatic refraction of light within droplets of rain in the air.","Any prismatic refraction of light showing a spectrum of colours."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Multicolored, especially if in rainbow order.","Made up of several races or ethnicities, or (more broadly) of several cultural or ideological factions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainbow"},{"term":"fish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A typically cold-blooded vertebrate animal that lives in water, moving with the help of fins and breathing with gills; any vertebrate that is not a tetrapod.","Any vertebrate, including tetrapods."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A period of time spent fishing.","An instance of seeking something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fish"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Rainbow Fish","blocks":[{"text":"The Rainbow Fish is a children's picture book drawn and written by Swiss author and illustrator Marcus Pfister; it was translated into English by J. Alison James. The book is best known for its message about selfishness and sharing and for the distinctive shiny foil scales of the Rainbow Fish. Decode Entertainment turned the story into an animated television series of the same name, which aired on the HBO Family television channel in the United States and Teletoon in Canada from 1999 until 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Rainbow_fish_original_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rainbow_Fish"},{"title":"Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"A rainbow is an optical phenomenon caused by refraction, internal reflection and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a continuous spectrum of light appearing in the sky. The rainbow takes the form of a multicoloured circular arc. Rainbows caused by sunlight always appear in the section of sky directly opposite the sun. Rainbows can be caused by many forms of airborne water. These include not only rain, but also mist, spray, and airborne dew."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg/330px-Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow"},{"title":"Fish","blocks":[{"text":"A fish is an aquatic, anamniotic, gill-bearing vertebrate animal with a tough cranium to protect the brain, but lacking limbs with digits. Fish can be grouped into the more basal jawless fish and the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. Tetrapods are descended from fish, so in a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. To treat fish as a monophyletic group, one would have to classify tetrapods as a clade/subgroup of specialized fish, which would make \"fish\" and \"vertebrates\" synonyms. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Balantiocheilos_melanopterus_-_Karlsruhe_Zoo_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rainbow in Moshav Aviel, Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_41259_Israeli_Rainbow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/500px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/1280px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg/500px-Ring-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_%2852910%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A colourful rainbow and ring-billed gull","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARing-billed_gull_and_a_rainbow_(52910).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Raindrop_optics.jpg/500px-Raindrop_optics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Raindrop_optics.jpg/500px-Raindrop_optics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Definition on angles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaindrop_optics.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Regenbogen_%C3%BCber_dem_Lipno-Stausee.JPG/500px-Regenbogen_%C3%BCber_dem_Lipno-Stausee.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Regenbogen_%C3%BCber_dem_Lipno-Stausee.JPG/1280px-Regenbogen_%C